• G3 (“Deliver Resources”):
 – G3.1: “Perform Normal Delivery” – the normal sequence (e.g. navigate to destination, deliver).
 – G3.2: “Handle Low Battery in Delivery” – when battery falls below 30%, the robot returns the resource to a checkpoint, reassigns remaining delivery, and (if needed) triggers an alert.
  – Runtime annotation for G3 is FALLBACK(G3.1, G3.2).

Because the collection must be completed prior to delivery, G1 is executed sequentially (using “;”) and the children of G2 and G3 are combined in an AND relationship.

