| AT7   | Deliver Resources                 | AND        | Destination Location  | 1                | The resource is delivered by the robot at the destination.                                             |
| AT8   | Return to Checkpoint              | AND        | Checkpoint            | 1                | The robot returns the resource to a checkpoint if battery is low during delivery.                        |
| AT9   | Assign Remaining Delivery         | AND        | Checkpoint            | 1                | The robot informs the control center to reassign the remaining delivery task.                           |
| AT10  | Trigger Alert and Report          | AND        | Control Center        | 1                | If the resource cannot be safely returned to the checkpoint, an alert is triggered.                      |

──────────────────────────────
Summary of Logical Relationships

• G1 -> G2 and G3  
 – Relation: AND, Sequential (using “;”)  
 – Justification: The collection phase (G2) must be fully executed before the delivery phase (G3) can begin.

• G2 -> G2.1 and G2.2  
 – Relation: AND, Fallback (using FALLBACK operator)  
 – Justification: Normal collection (G2.1) is the preferred execution, but if battery drops below 10%, the fallback branch (G2.2) is activated.

• G3 -> G3.1 and G3.2  
 – Relation: AND, Fallback (using FALLBACK operator)  
 – Justification: Normal delivery (G3.1) is preferred; however, if battery falls below 30%, the fallback branch (G3.2) ensures safe handling.

• G2.1 -> AT1, AT2, AT3  
 – Relation: AND, Sequential  
 – Justification: The tasks must occur in sequence: navigate, request, and then wait for retrieval.

• G2.2 -> AT4, AT5  
 – Relation: AND, Sequential  
 – Justification: The battery low handling during collection involves returning to the charging station and reassigning the mission.

• G3.1 -> AT6, AT7  
 – Relation: AND, Sequential  
 – Justification: Normal delivery is achieved by first navigating to the destination and then delivering the resources.

• G3.2 -> AT8, AT9, AT10  
 – Relation: AND, Sequential  
 – Justification: When battery is low during delivery, the resource is returned to a checkpoint, the remaining delivery is reassigned, and if necessary, an alert is triggered.

